 "title": "Keith County Highway Department",
 "text": "Keith County Highway Department\nATTENTION! You are using an outdated browser . For a better experience using our website, please upgrade to a modern browser by clicking on one of the icons to the right.\nMenu\nHome\nOffices\nAssessor\nAssessor Home\nAttorney\nAttorney Home\nBoard of Commissioners\nBoard of Commissioners Home\nClerk\nClerk Home\nCounty Court (Judge's Office)\nDistrict Court\nDistrict Court Home\nElection\nElection Home\nExtension Office (Keith/Arthur/University of Nebraska Lincoln)\nEmergency Management\nEmergency Management Home\nHighway Department\nHighway Department Home\nJail\nJail Home\nPlanning and Zoning\nProbation - District 11\nRegister of Deeds\nRegister of Deeds Home\nSheriff\nSheriff's Office Home\nSurveyor\nSurveyor Home\nNebraska State Surveyors Office\nNational Geodetic Survey\nNational Weather Service\nFEMA Flood Zone Maps\nProfessional Surveyors Association of Nebraska\nTreasurer\nTreasurer Home\nVeterans\nVisitor's Committee\nWeed Control\nWeed Control Home\n911\n911 Home\nCounty History\nHistory of Keith County\nHistory of Ogallala\nHistory of Brule\nHistory of Paxton\nHistory of Lake McConaughy and Lake Communities\nHistory Photos 1\nHistory Photos 2\nHistorical Photos\nOFFICIAL AND EMPLOYEE DIRECTORY\nEmployees\nHome » Offices » Highway Department\nHighway Department Home\n2024 - 1 & 6 Year Road Map\nRoad Right of Way Permit\nSnow Removal Policy\nPriority Snow Route Map\nCulvert Policy\nNebraska Department of Transportation\nGIS Workshop\nNebraska Association of County Officials\nKeith County Highway Department\n|\nThomas Wilbur, Highway Superintendent\n202 West Riverdale Drive\nOgallala NE 69153\nPhone: (308) 284-6601\nFax: (308) 284-6950\nroads@keithcountyne.gov\nThe Highway Department responsibilities include road and bridge maintenance which consists of signing, graveling, mowing, paving maintenance, drainage, snow removal, along with bridge inspections and culvert repair/ replacement. The Highway Superintendent works with 3 foreman and 14 employees in 3 grading districts to maintain over 800 miles of roads in Keith County. This consists of 70 miles of paved roads and 640 miles of gravel roads as well as over 90 miles of minimum maintenance roads. It is also the responsibility of the Highway Superintendent to prepare the annual report, annual budget, one and six year road plan and report directly to the County Commissioners. Keith County also promotes good partnership by Interlocal agreements with Lincoln, Arthur, Deuel, Garden and Perkins Counties as well as the City of Ogallala.\nCitizen Portal: https://keithcountyne.novokiosk.com/citizen/\nMission Statement\nTo provide and maintain, in cooperation with public and private organizations, a safe, reliable, affordable, environmentally compatible and coordinated countywide transportation system for the movement of people and goods.\nOffice Hours:\nMonday – Friday\n7:00 a.m. to 3:30 p.m.\nClosed Saturdays, Sundays, and Holidays\n********************************\nHighway Department Employees Luke Nielsen and Hap Staman at the 2024 Touch A Truck Event during the Indian Summer Rendezvous!\n2016 Copyright Keith County Nebraska\nPhone: (308) 284-4726 Fax: (308) 284-6277\nPowered By revize. Login\nTop",
